-- title:
--   Chain rule: δ f = (df/dt) δ t for a uniformiser t
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $F$ be fields with $F$ a $K$-algebra, $K$ perfect, and let $x \in F$ be such that $F$ is algebraic over the intermediate field $K(x)$ generated by $x$. Let $v$ be a place of $F$ over $K$, i.e. a valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of $K$, distinct from $F$ itself, and whose ring is a principal ideal ring; let $t \in F$ satisfy $v.\mathrm{ord}\,t = 1$, where $\mathrm{ord}$ is minus the logarithm of the associated adic valuation on $\mathbb{Z}^{m0}$, so that $t$ is a uniformiser at $v$. Let $\delta : F \to F$ be a $K$-derivation and $f \in F$. Then $\delta f = c \cdot \delta t$, where $c =$ `Place.diffCoeff t (KaehlerDifferential.D K F f)` is, by definition, a chosen $g \in F$ with $\mathrm{d}f = g \cdot \mathrm{d}t$ in $\Omega_{F/K}$ if such a $g$ exists, and $0$ otherwise; thus $c$ plays the role of the derivative $df/dt$.
--
--   This is the chain rule in a one-variable function field: every $K$-derivation of $F$ is the multiple by $\delta t$ of the coordinate derivative $d/dt$ at a uniformiser $t$. It is used to pass between an explicitly given derivation of a modular function field and the derivative with respect to a local parameter, and is cited in the analysis of $q$-expansions at a place through [`ModularCurve.jGeomGen_sub_mul_div_mem_and_evalAt_eq_of_coe_eq_thetaL_div`](thm.html#ModularCurve.jGeomGen_sub_mul_div_mem_and_evalAt_eq_of_coe_eq_thetaL_div).
